00:23:35.700 --> 00:23:37.800
Let's head back to the UI.

00:23:37.800 --> 00:23:40.920
Just couple of other things
that I wanted to mention is

00:23:40.920 --> 00:23:48.330
that the prompt for these
LLM models are our scripts

00:23:48.330 --> 00:23:50.580
that are written in
our code itself.

00:23:50.580 --> 00:23:54.450
So if we'll go to -- go back
to our code and I can show you

00:23:54.450 --> 00:23:57.690
like an extract
memories prompt file.

00:23:57.690 --> 00:24:02.400
So here you can see that we are
deliberately giving instructions

00:24:02.400 --> 00:24:07.050
to the LLM that these are the
four different type of memories

00:24:07.050 --> 00:24:10.050
that you can extract,
and we have given

00:24:10.050 --> 00:24:12.810
like detailed information
in the prompt

00:24:12.810 --> 00:24:14.700
like what should
be the structure

00:24:14.700 --> 00:24:18.810
of those memories rules
according to like which rules

00:24:18.810 --> 00:24:22.560
and examples that what kind of
a memory would be classified

00:24:22.560 --> 00:24:24.960
as fact, what would be
classified as procedural,

00:24:24.960 --> 00:24:29.370
what would be classified as
episodic, and similarly,

00:24:29.370 --> 00:24:32.820
prompts have been given -- the
prompt, there are rules given

00:24:32.820 --> 00:24:37.980
to this prompt that what kind
of turn should be extracted.

00:24:37.980 --> 00:24:41.220
So for an example, if my
turn just has greetings

00:24:41.220 --> 00:24:45.090
to the assistant, those
turns would not be extracted

00:24:45.090 --> 00:24:46.020
as a fact.

00:24:46.020 --> 00:24:50.520
So if I'm just saying hello, hi,
good morning, good afternoon,

00:24:50.520 --> 00:24:53.520
so those turns would
not be extracted.

00:24:53.520 --> 00:24:55.800
Now let's look at
how summarization,

00:24:55.800 --> 00:24:57.540
auto-summarization works.

00:24:57.540 --> 00:25:02.070
So as I mentioned, just for this
demo, we have set that cadence

00:25:02.070 --> 00:25:06.180
as five turns, so as soon as
